; spec/assets/chicago12.art -- InitechOS "Chicago 12" system-font strike, the
; LOCKED hand-authored source (bead initech-tdnl.33, slice 1). Rule 8: this file
; is the contract; spec/assets/chicago12.h is GENERATED from it by
; tools/font_art2h.c (make gen-chicago12; test-chicago-art proves the committed
; header is byte-identical to a fresh transcription).
;
; PROVENANCE (Law 1 honesty) -- two different kinds of data live here:
;   METRICS (the "lb"/"aw" numbers on every glyph line) are MEASUREMENTS of the
;     real System 7.0.1 Chicago 12 strike, NFNT 5478 (../system7-decomp
;     goldens/resources/NFNT_5478.bin, owTable: high byte = left bearing lb,
;     low byte = advance aw; specs/fonts/chicago.md "Advance-width table",
;     specs/fonts/font-manager.md Sec 1.1). Functional metrics are citable
;     (chicago.md "Clean-room boundary"). The missing-glyph line carries the
;     owTable missing entry (index lastChar+1: lb 0, aw 10; font-manager.md
;     Sec 5). Copied mechanically from the owTable bytes by a scratch script.
;   GLYPH ART (the '#' maps) is HAND-AUTHORED for this file, to the Chicago
;     typeface DESIGN: 2-px vertical stems, 1-px horizontals, cap and ascender
;     height 9 rows (rows 3..11), x-height 7 rows (rows 5..11), descenders 3
;     rows (rows 12..14) -- design proportions read off rendered real-Mac
;     screenshots (goldens/captures/s7_menu_file.png: "Edit" caps rows 5..13 of
;     the 20-px bar, 'e' 7 rows, 'g' 3 rows below the baseline). The art was
;     NOT transcribed, traced or copied from the real strike bitmap
;     (chicago12_strike.png / the NFNT bitImage are Apple IP and were not
;     opened while authoring); they may be used only as a diff oracle after the
;     fact. The owTable lb/aw and the NFNT locationTable glyph-image WIDTHS
;     (extents only, no pixel data) were consulted to size each ink box.
;     After the first draft, the real strike was used AS A DIFF ORACLE (per-
;     glyph ink row extents and ink counts only): it flagged p/q descending
;     2 rows not 3, t starting on row 3, and the vertical placement / weight of
;     # $ % * - / < = > @ \ _ ` { | } ~; those glyphs were then REDRAWN by
;     hand to the corrected extents (no pixel was copied).
;     Earlier v0 shapes (spec/assets/chicago8x16.h, hand-authored) were
;     the starting point; every glyph was redrawn to the 9-row cap height and
;     to its real advance (M W m w and the narrow i l ' ! . , : ; included).
;
; FORMAT: one block per glyph, codes 0x20..0x7E in order, then "missing".
;   glyph <code|missing> lb <n> aw <n>
;   16 rows, each exactly aw characters: '#' = ink, '.' = paper. Row 12 is the
;   first row below the baseline (ascent 12); row 15 is the leading row and is
;   always blank. The cell is the advance: the renderer paints exactly aw
;   columns. The leftmost ink column of every inked glyph MUST equal lb (the
;   transcriber fails loud otherwise), so the art is checked against the real
;   bearing, and no ink may sit at or beyond aw.
; ASCII-clean (Rule 12). Lines starting ';' are comments.
